  "summary": "sudo vulnerability",
  "details": "USN-8895-1 fixed a vulnerability in Sudo. This update provides the\ncorresponding updates for Ubuntu 18.04 LTS and Ubuntu 20.04 LTS.\n\nOriginal advisory details:\n\nIt was discovered that Sudo did not properly handle time-based access\nrestrictions when sudoers rules used NOTBEFORE or NOTAFTER with\ntimestamps omitting the trailing timezone indicator. A local attacker\ncould possibly use this issue to execute commands outside the intended\ntime window by manipulating the TZ environment variable.",
